{"shortDescription":"Asia's diesel market stayed upbeat on Wednesday, although margins and timespreads declined, while jet fuel cash markets slipped into discounts for the first time since July last year.Traders were watching for more October spot offers, given limited selling interest emerging from Northeast Asia as o…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Asia's diesel market stayed upbeat on Wednesday, although margins and timespreads declined, while jet fuel cash markets slipped into discounts for the first time since July last year."]},{"type":"p","children":["Traders were watching for more October spot offers, given limited selling interest emerging from Northeast Asia as of the previous trading session and since late last week."]},{"type":"p","children":["However, concerns emerged over the outlook for simple and complex refining margins over the next two months, as crude premiums continue to gain."]},{"type":"p","children":["Refining margins (GO10SGCKMc1) declined to slightly below $70 a barrel, reversing some of the gains from the last two sessions."]},{"type":"p","children":["The 10 ppm sulphur gasoil cash differentials (GO10-SIN-DIF) inched down, tracking a softer market structure, with deals for higher sulphur grade prevalent."]},{"type":"p","children":["On the jet fuel front, trading-window discussions were slightly muted, though cash markets softened even further into discounts, tracking the easing backwardation in swap markets."]},{"type":"p","children":["The arbitrage window to the U.S. West Coast markets remained largely shut for most of the week."]},{"type":"p","children":["Regrade (JETREG10SGMc1) widened back to discounts of slightly more than $2 a barrel."]},{"type":"p","children":["SINGAPORE CASH DEALS"]},{"type":"p","children":["- Two gasoil deals, no jet fuel deals"]},{"type":"p","children":["INVENTORIES"]},{"type":"p","children":["- U.S. crude and fuel inventories fell last week, market sources said, citing data from the American Petroleum Institute released on Tuesday."]},{"type":"p","children":["NEWS"]},{"type":"p","children":["- Oil vessel transit costs through the Strait of Hormuz have escalated significantly after the ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/iran/","linkText":"Iran war"}},", led by a sharp climb in additional war risk premiums and cargo insurance costs, an executive from Emirates National Oil Company (ENOC) said on Wednesday."]},{"type":"p","children":["- The supply of fuel oil is under control despite refiners switching more production to higher-margin middle distillates, a senior executive from Saudi Arabia's Yasref Company said on Wednesday."]},{"type":"p","children":["- India's refinery capacity utilisation has been at 105% to 108% over the last six months, a senior official from refiner Mangalore Refinery and Petrochemicals ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NSE:MRPL","text":"NSE:MRPL"}}," said on Wednesday, adding that higher diesel demand is pushing refiners to prioritise diesel over jet fuel."]},{"type":"p","children":["- Six commodity vessels transited the Strait of Hormuz on Tuesday, down from nine a day earlier and below the 10-day average of about 12, preliminary shipping data showed on Wednesday."]},{"type":"p","children":["PRICES"]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["MIDDLE DISTILLATES"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["CASH ($/BBL)"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["ASIA CLOSE"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Change"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Prev Close"]}]},